  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14183030/assets/e046aafb09255a579c76a48f0f422627761a19451ae36a053424a8ac8a3332f7.png)\n\nWhat is the diameter of a circle with a circumference of $\\frac{5\\pi }{2}?$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the circumference $C=\\pi d$ and solve for $d.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\ \\frac{5\\pi }{2} & =\\pi d \\\\ d & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2\\pi } \\\\ d & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
